{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7z7zMQumNjToiNv4iA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`{% static %}`, `{% get_static_prefix %}`, `{% get_media_prefix %}` and the storage classes now prepend the current `SCRIPT_NAME` to a relative `STATIC_URL` or `MEDIA_URL`. I haven't added a test that exercises this directly.\n\nThe change is in `django/conf/__init__.py`. When `settings.STATIC_URL` or `settings.MEDIA_URL` is read, a value that doesn't start with `/`, `http://` or `https://` gets `get_script_prefix()` put in front of it. Absolute paths and full URLs pass through unchanged. The prefixed value is cached with the other settings. Because everything reads these two settings through `django.conf.settings`, I didn't touch the template tags or storage classes themselves.\n\nI ran `settings_tests`, `staticfiles_tests` and `file_storage`, and 4 tests fail with this change:\n\n- **Failures:** the four `test_setting_changed` tests in `file_storage` now fail. They compare `base_url` against the raw override value `overridden_media_url/`, and `base_url` now returns `/overridden_media_url/`. That is the new behaviour working as intended, so I expect those assertions to need updating. I didn't edit them, per the rules.\n- **Errors:** the 2 errors are live-server tests (`StaticLiveServerView` and `FileLikeObjectTestCase`) that can't bind their port in this environment. They fail the same way on a clean checkout."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3157,"cache_read_input_tokens":23401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3157},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8420bb3-4b91-4a1e-939f-464f66ba5e73","uuid":